---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Project | Trajectory Copilot" description="Project overview, methodology, and success criteria.">
  <section class="space-y-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Trajectory Copilot</h1>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Problem statement</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">As mission design moves deeper into the cislunar environment, trajectory optimization, rendezvous, formation flying, and low-thrust transfers are becoming more complex. Large language models show strong reasoning and coding ability, but their usefulness as engineering copilots for astrodynamics remains largely unexplored.</p>
        <p class="text-slate-300">The central question is not whether AI can replace astrodynamics tools, but whether it can help engineers formulate, analyze, and optimize trajectories more effectively.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Why it matters</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">Space operations are expanding beyond Earth orbit, and mission planning in the Earth-Moon system demands both technical expertise and extensive computational analysis. If AI can support trajectory design in a trustworthy way, it could accelerate analysis, lower barriers to entry, and improve engineering productivity.</p>
        <p class="text-slate-300">This matters for future cislunar operations, autonomous rendezvous, and space domain awareness workflows where engineers need fast iteration with physically valid results.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Research question</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">Can large language models effectively support spacecraft trajectory design by interacting with physics-based mission analysis tools?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Methodology</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">The workflow combines large language models such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and future frontier systems with physics-based tools including GMAT, Python astrodynamics libraries, and numerical optimization frameworks.</p>
        <p class="text-slate-300">The AI system generates candidate mission designs, optimization approaches, and simulation workflows, while traditional astrodynamics tools provide physical validation and performance evaluation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Current scope</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">This class project focuses on reproducing and explaining solutions from published spacecraft trajectory optimization research. Representative problems include orbital rendezvous, formation reconfiguration, low-thrust transfers, relative motion dynamics, and spacecraft formation flight.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">This is the first and only phase for the current project, and it serves as a foundation for future cislunar mission design work if the research continues beyond the class.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">System flow</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col items-center gap-4 md:flex-row md:justify-between">
        <div class="flow-node pulse">Prompt</div>
        <div class="text-orbital">→</div>
        <div class="flow-node pulse">Plan</div>
        <div class="text-orbital">→</div>
        <div class="flow-node pulse">Simulate</div>
        <div class="text-orbital">→</div>
        <div class="flow-node pulse">Validate</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Milestones</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>1.</strong> Build a benchmark dataset from known astrodynamics problems.</li>
          <li><strong>2.</strong> Test multiple LLMs on problem setup, explanation, and workflow generation.</li>
          <li><strong>3.</strong> Compare AI-generated solutions against known analytical and numerical results.</li>
          <li><strong>4.</strong> Evaluate whether LLMs can assist an engineer using GMAT or related tools.</li>
          <li><strong>5.</strong> Summarize findings and identify the most promising directions for thesis work.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Success metrics</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li>Accuracy of solutions relative to known benchmarks</li>
          <li>Ability to explain and set up optimization problems correctly</li>
          <li>Quality of generated GMAT or simulation workflows</li>
          <li>Consistency across multiple models</li>
          <li>Usefulness to a human engineer working through trajectory design</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Data and restrictions</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">This project uses public and synthetic data only. The benchmark set is based on published research and non-sensitive reference problems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Long-term vision</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300">This class project is the foundation for a future master’s thesis on AI-assisted mission planning in more complex dynamical environments, including CR3BP, Earth-Moon trajectory design, cislunar rendezvous, and autonomous mission planning under uncertainty.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
